issue_context.body:
As part of the LFX mentorship, I try to integrate the Pod Security Admission with Kyverno to provide native admission enforcement for finer-grained controls. I presented a demo at [the sig-auth meeting](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=etGq-IKxZRk&list=PL69nYSiGNLP0VMOZ-V7-5AchXTHAQFzJw&index=2). For design specification, please refer to [Extending Pod Security Admission](https://github.com/kyverno/KDP/pull/22).

One challenge we are facing now is to get details from the [CheckResult](https://github.com/kubernetes/pod-security-admission/blob/767140a93fb0bb7225966c475eef70294322d79a/policy/checks.go#L65-L82). We are thinking to add an additional field `RestrictedFields` which contains the forbidden paths and its values. For example:

```
{
  "Allowed":false,
  "ForbiddenReason":"non-default capabilities",
  "ForbiddenDetail":"containers "init-container-nginx-host-network", "nginx-host-network" must not include "SYS_ADMIN", "SYS_NICE" in securityContext.capabilities.add",

  // Fields to add
  "RestrictedFields":[
   {
     "Path":"spec.containers[*].securityContext.capabilities.add",
     "ContainerName": "nginx-host-network",
     "ForbiddenValues":[
      "SYS_ADMIN",
      "SYS_NICE"
     ]
   },
   {
     "Path":"spec.initContainers[*].securityContext.capabilities.add",
     "ContainerName": "init-container-nginx-host-network",
     "ForbiddenValues":[
      "SYS_ADMIN",
      "SYS_NICE"
     ]
   }
  ]
}
```
Would it be possible to add these into the `CheckResult`? Or is there any plan of adding such? We’d like to contribute if this sounds valid.

